                        Blomefield</persName> on fol. cclviii. Blomefield gives an account of how
                     the book came into his possession in 1726.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Dawson Turner bought it for <persName
                        role="fmo">Robert Sparrow</persName> of Worlingham from <persName role="fmo"
                        >Mr Stevenson</persName> of Norwich, 5 December 1816. This was the last
                     known provenance according to the supplement to Medieval Libraries of Great
                     Britain (1987). The corresponding Medieval Libraries of Great Britain Index card
                     also notes the following: 'Details under "Pressmarks" and "Owners" recorded by
                     Dawson Turner in his copy of Chron. Nuremb, now [c.1970?] belonging to Mrs
                     Murray, Cudlington, Horndean, Hants.'</provenance>
